---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Technology | Blutech Building AI and IoT" description="How Blutech combines Bluetooth edge control, LoRaWAN building data, 4G/IP backhaul, Halo, Core and open building-system integration." canonicalPath="/technology">
  <section class="page-hero tech-intro"><div class="shell"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><span>Technology</span></div><div class="kicker">System architecture</div><h1>Edge for response. Cloud for visibility and management.</h1><p>Blutech products often use more than one protocol because the building needs more than one kind of behaviour: immediate local action, dependable long-range data and central operating control.</p></div></section>

  <section class="protocol-story"><div class="shell"><div class="protocol-grid"><article><span>01 · Edge</span><h2>Bluetooth for local control</h2><p>A nearby sensor can control an assigned light, indicator, buzzer or edge module directly. The time-sensitive path stays within the building zone and can continue without an internet round trip.</p><ul><li>Immediate response</li><li>Local grouping and logic</li><li>Offline resilience</li></ul></article><article><span>02 · Field network</span><h2>LoRaWAN for data and settings</h2><p>Low-power field devices report events, measurements and health across floors and properties. Downlinks carry approved settings back to the device.</p><ul><li>Long-range building coverage</li><li>Low-power sensing</li><li>Status, events and configuration</li></ul></article><article><span>03 · Backhaul</span><h2>4G or IP to Blutech Core</h2><p>Gateways connect the LoRaWAN estate through 4G, Ethernet or approved networks, allowing projects to work within different customer IT boundaries.</p><ul><li>4G, Ethernet or Wi-Fi</li><li>Gateway health</li><li>Cloud, private-cloud or on-premise options</li></ul></article></div></div></section>

  <section class="architecture"><div class="shell architecture-grid"><div><div class="kicker">One coordinated data path</div><h2>Every layer has a responsibility.</h2><p>Hardware is selected around the real operating signal. Core manages the infrastructure. Halo turns the result into a building view. APIs connect approved information to BMS, FM, ESG, government or customer systems.</p></div><div class="architecture-stack"><div><span>Owners & operators</span><b>Blutech Halo</b><p>Floorplans · alerts · reports · authorised controls</p></div><div><span>IoT operations</span><b>Blutech Core</b><p>Registry · provisioning · health · rules · APIs</p></div><div><span>Gateway & integration</span><b>LoRaWAN + 4G / IP</b><p>Data · settings · payloads · building interfaces</p></div><div><span>Building edge</span><b>Bluetooth + field I/O</b><p>Immediate sensing · local logic · direct response</p></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="sensing"><div class="shell"><div class="compact-title"><div class="kicker">Sensing by purpose</div><h2>Accurate sensing first. AI where it improves the result.</h2><p>Blutech selects thermal, PIR, mmWave, environmental, contact or spatial sensing according to the space, privacy requirement and decision the building needs to make.</p></div><div class="sense-grid"><article><h3>Thermal sensing</h3><p>Privacy-preserving occupancy and spatial signals without conventional identifiable video.</p></article><article><h3>mmWave fusion</h3><p>Richer movement and safety understanding when combined with thermal sensing and local AI.</p></article><article><h3>PIR & environmental</h3><p>Efficient motion, temperature, humidity, PM2.5 and other operational inputs.</p></article><article><h3>Contacts & RS485</h3><p>Bring useful signals from doors, pumps, meters and third-party equipment into the IoT layer.</p></article></div></div></section>

  <section class="tech-cta"><div class="shell cta-panel"><div><div class="kicker">For consultants and property teams</div><h2>Start with the control sequence and integration boundary.</h2><p>We can map the right field signal, local response, wireless path and software handover around the building.</p></div><a class="button" href="/contact">Discuss the architecture</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
